---
// Cookie Policy. The marketing site is static Astro and sets no tracking or
// advertising cookies; only Stripe (during checkout) and Netlify (hosting /
// security) may set strictly-necessary cookies. Verified: no analytics/ad
// scripts in the source.
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { legal } from "../lib/legal.mjs";
---
<LegalPage
  title="Cookie Policy — Better Business Web"
  description="How Better Business Web uses cookies — in short, no tracking or advertising cookies."
  heading="Cookie Policy"
>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files a website can store in your browser. This page
    explains how we use them. The short version: <strong>we don't use cookies to
    track you or to advertise.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies we use</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is a static site with <strong>no analytics, advertising, or
    tracking cookies</strong>, and we don't build profiles of visitors. We don't
    show a cookie banner because we don't set non-essential cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Essential third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>
    A couple of trusted providers may set strictly-necessary cookies so the site
    can work and stay secure:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stripe</strong> — when you go through checkout, Stripe may set
      cookies needed for secure payment processing and fraud prevention.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Netlify</strong> — our host may use essential cookies and logs for
      security and to serve the site reliably.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These are essential to providing the service and aren't used to track you for
    advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time. Note
    that blocking the essential cookies above may stop checkout from working
    properly.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add cookies — for example, analytics — we'll update this page and,
    where required, ask for your consent first. Questions? Email
    <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
